:name: stm32-baremetal-boot
:description: STM32F103C8 Blue Pill running the bare-metal boot firmware

# Usage (interactive):
#   renode renode/bluepill.resc               # loads build/firmware.elf
#   $elf=@build/control.elf; i @renode/bluepill.resc
# The robot suite sets $elf itself.

using sysbus
$elf ?= @build/firmware.elf

mach create "bluepill"
machine LoadPlatformDescription $ORIGIN/bluepill.repl

showAnalyzer usart1

macro reset
"""
    sysbus LoadELF $elf
    # Renode has no BOOT0 pin and does not alias flash at 0x0000_0000, so the
    # vector table's location is stated explicitly. LoadELF would also infer
    # it from the lowest loaded segment; being explicit makes the claim visible.
    sysbus.cpu VectorTableOffset 0x08000000
"""

runMacro $reset
